# expect: hang_empty_handle.or:20:0 - unknown identifier `handle`
# This HUNG THE COMPILER FOREVER, found by tools/fuzz.sh.
#
# A `handle` with an empty body leaves the body parser starting at the NEXT
# declaration, which sits at the same column, so the dedent rule does not fire
# and the second `handle` is read as a statement. That statement is
# `Log.msg(text: text)`, a method call whose argument list stops dead on the
# `:` - and psr_parse_postfix's argument loop had no no-progress guard, so it
# spun on a cursor that never moved. Fifth instance of that class of bug
# (map literal, list literal, psr_parse_call, the statement loop, this).
#
# What matters here is that the compiler ANSWERS. The message it gives is the
# ordinary one for a word used where no such name is bound.

effect Log:
    msg: function(text: text) -> text

handle Log.msg(text: text) -> text:

handle Log.msg(text: text) -> text:
    resume("ok")

define main() -> int:
    1
